# tools/m/mycelium_testament_bron_witness.rish — a named constellation's certificate travels as a readable
# record and still proves itself against its own roster offline (r3, the Testament travel rung).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) · Mycelium consensus · Testament · rung r3.
# r1 sealed a reading into a Testament and verified it offline from the roster names alone; r2 carried the
# roll's fault tolerance into that offline certificate. Yet the certificate still lived in memory. r3 lets
# the whole Testament cross as `format testament-v1` bytes — one `ship <name>` line per roster ship (the NAME
# only, since a ship's key is a pure function of its name), the shared claim named once, and one
# `member <node-hex> <sig-hex>` line per sealing voice; render/parse is a fixed point.
#
# The crux this witness proves is THE NAMED BINDING SURVIVES THE WIRE: a testament-v1 record states NO
# threshold and carries the constellation's NAMES, so parse boots the roster, derives the Byzantine threshold
# from its size, and re-runs r1's verify — a stranger's valid voice refuses NotMember, a thin quorum refuses
# BelowQuorum, a tampered ship name re-derives a different key so a real signer stops being a member
# (NotMember), the same teeth r1 proved, now across the wire. Composes testament + constel + chorus + voucher
# public API only, editing none; siloed dev fixtures, demo seeds — no key, funds, network, real value.
#
# Scope: active-designing/date/20260813/20260813-135126_mycelium-testament-named-quorum-certificate-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mycelium_testament_bron_witness.rish

say "mycelium-testament-bron: Language EN — a belief a keeper cannot hand to another is only a local reading; this round lets a named constellation's whole certificate cross as a format testament-v1 record, carrying the roster names so a recipient boots the constellation and knows the verdict true, holding only the text."
say "mycelium-testament-bron: Style Radiant — the record names the roster and the seal, states no threshold, and proves itself after the crossing against the constellation its own names define; render and parse are a fixed point, and no stranger's valid voice, no thin quorum, no tampered name ever passes for the fleet's own."
say "mycelium-testament-bron: Lens TAME — a purpose-built bounded reader (max_record 8192, one ship line per roster ship, one member line per voice), never a general parser; the threshold is DERIVED from the booted roster's names, never a number the record states about itself; composes testament + constel + chorus + voucher public API only; ship names can never parse as a live-network @p; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/testament_bron"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/testament_bron.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-testament-bron: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-testament-bron: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-testament-bron: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "fixed point" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the fixed-point claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "proves itself OFFLINE after the crossing" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the offline-after-crossing claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "refuses NotMember" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the stranger-binding refusal claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "BelowQuorum" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the thin-quorum refusal claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "tampered ship name" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the tampered-name refusal claim missing"

# The r1 crux stands at the door — a travel rung means nothing unless the in-memory certificate still
# verifies offline against the constellation its names define.
let r1 = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/testament.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/testament && mycelium/bin/testament 2>&1"]
assert r1.ok else "mycelium-testament-bron: the Testament r1 crux is not GREEN"
assert r1.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-testament-bron: the Testament r1 did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-testament-bron: GREEN — a five-ship named constellation's certificate travels as a format testament-v1 record and parses back byte-for-byte, booting the roster from the names alone to prove itself offline against its own derived threshold; a stranger's valid voice refuses NotMember, a thin quorum BelowQuorum, a tampered ship name NotMember, and a bad header · unknown field · missing field · bad hex each refuse; the Testament r1 crux stands at the door. The named verdict is a portable object a keeper hands another keeper."
